# wado-relay behind Caddy — TLS for the relay, decided 2026-10-02 (WADO_PLAN.md Decision Log).
#
# Caddy gets and renews the certificate itself; the relay stays plain HTTP on localhost and has
# no TLS code. Browsers then reach it as wss://relay.example.com — set that as the relay URL in
# the client, and WADO_RELAY_URL=wss://relay.example.com on each daemon.
#
# Install: put this at /etc/caddy/Caddyfile with your domain, point the domain's A/AAAA record at
# the server, open ports 80 and 443, and run the relay with deploy/relay/wado-relay.service.
#
# WebSockets need nothing extra: reverse_proxy passes the upgrade through. Caddy sets
# X-Forwarded-For, which is why the relay runs with --trust-proxy — and why it must listen on
# 127.0.0.1 only, so nothing can reach it without going through here.

relay.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:4000
}
